---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Callout from "../components/Callout.astro";
import { identity } from "../data/portfolio";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="About Hamood Siddiqui, a Python and Full-Stack Developer focused on backend systems, AI integrations and automation."
  path="/about/"
>
  <header class="page-hero">
    <div class="shell">
      <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
      <h1>I like the part where software has to meet reality.</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        {identity.positioning} My strongest work sits at the connection points: a model and a
        database, a client and a service, live media and connection state, or a repeated manual
        process and a reliable automation.
      </p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell split-layout">
      <div class="sticky-label">
        <p class="eyebrow">How I think</p>
        <h2>Systems before spectacle.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          A polished interface matters, but it cannot rescue an unclear workflow or a weak system
          boundary. I start by understanding who is trying to do what, which state needs to be
          trusted, and where failure should become visible.
        </p>
        <h3>Make the path inspectable</h3>
        <p>
          AiSQL exposes the SQL between the natural-language question and the result. The speech
          workflow separates recording from processing. The consultation application separates
          controllers, services and persistence. Those choices make the system easier to explain,
          test and improve.
        </p>
        <h3>Separate current evidence from future architecture</h3>
        <p>
          Real engineering includes knowing what has been implemented and what is still a design
          proposal. The Fill Masjid case study therefore treats the current WebRTC relay and the
          proposed SFU-backed architecture as different milestones.
        </p>
        <h3>Review security as part of the product</h3>
        <p>
          Upload boundaries, credentials, access control and privacy are not finishing touches.
          The case studies name security limitations directly and explain the next engineering
          step without turning the portfolio into a vulnerability showcase.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Callout
    title="Clear problem definition, practical engineering and accountable delivery."
    copy="That is the standard I bring to backend, AI, automation and full-stack work."
    href="/contact/"
    action="Contact Hamood"
  />
</BaseLayout>
